WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's what people
are talking about.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.169 line:92%
You guys, today President Trump

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
gave a big speech
on national security.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.207
He focused on the three biggest
threats to our country --

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
Russia, North Korea,
and Omarosa.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:15.682 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.649 size:78% position:39% line:92%
At one point he said,

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We will never
lose sight of our values

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:22.622
and their capacity
to inspire, uplift, and renew."

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then he realized someone left
an old Obama speech

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the teleprompter.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:31.097
"That doesn't sound like me
at all. What just happened?

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wall.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on, Donald, improvise."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.275 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Covfefe.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
Once again it seemed like
Trump's mouth

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.378 line:92%
was getting a little dry.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know he's been having
that problem.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where he's like --
[ Laughs ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know -- United Shtates.
-Blesh United Shtates?

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, because his mouth
is getting dry.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Reallish.
-Well anyways, take a look.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.455 line:92%
His mouth is getting a little...

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where we are going
in the years ahead.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.528 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Lips smacking ]

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Ugh!

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I lost my appetite
forever. Okay.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:14.474 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:18.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like a baby trying solids
for the first time.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wonder if he remembered
his water this time.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.923 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Did he have any water?

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Calm down! Hey!

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Come on!
-I don't understand.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.328 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Who's talking to him?

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:38.898
Someone tell him he can't drink
water like that.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.432 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:42.168
That ought to really strike some
fear into our enemies.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.637 line:92%
"Don't you dare mess with us."

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.473 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.374 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ah! Wa-Wa!

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how a baby drinks
out of a sippy cup.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ah, yummy.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.182 size:78% position:39% line:92%
This is pretty crazy.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was revealed
that the Pentagon

00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:02.689
had a top secret program
to investigate UFOs and aliens.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which is why
Trump announced plans

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
to build a dome over the Earth
and make E.T. pay for it.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:13.199 line:92%
"That seems like my speech."

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:16.069 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:16.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What's going on?

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:21.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why would he do --
-I saw that yesterday --

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
No idea.
-Come on.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.611
Even if he grabbed it, drank it,
and threw it away.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:27.046
-I wouldn't care!
-That's so much tougher than...

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just throw the water
in your face.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.750
-...the double-handed baby sip.
-Better than that.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just pick it up, squirt it
like a Gatorade bottle.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give him a sports bottle.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With the sports bottle,
you just go...

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:39.225 size:88% position:44%
-Get like a boater bag.
Squeeze them in and out.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.093 line:92%
-Or like a camelback thing,

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a backpack with a tube
in his mouth.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wouldn't care.
Silly straw.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.399 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Did you guys see this?

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was
an 11-hour power outage

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the airport
in Atlanta yesterday.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:54.240
And people were stranded on
the tarmac for six hours.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:54.908 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Don't worry, though.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
Flight attendants
came through every hour

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a thimble-size cup of
room-temperature water.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.947 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That made them happy.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:04.617 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.819 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm sorry. Achoo!

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, I'm sorry.
Ooh, that spilled. Sorry.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the perfect size.
-But this is nice.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.795 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.431 line:92%
"They make glassware too large."

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:19.933 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:20.967 line:92%
Hey, this is kind of funny.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that Mark Hamill
and Ted Cruz

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
got into a Twitter fight over
net neutrality.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.606 line:92%
Got pretty heated at one point.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.273 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Hamill thought, "Oh, no.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.976 size:88% position:44%
Is this where I find out
Ted Cruz is my father?"

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.545 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.014
Speaking of Ted, did you see --
hear about this?

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last night Donald Trump Jr.
posted a photo of

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
himself and Ted Cruz on
Instagram with the caption,

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Some good friends decided
they would get me

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.356 line:92%
an early 40th birthday cake.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:47.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what birthday is complete
without an Obama cake?"

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, if you look closely
you can actually tell

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
what everyone in that photo
is thinking.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example,
Don Jr. is thinking,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.267 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"I'm nailing this smile.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:58.438
This is totally what a normal
person's smile looks like."

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.941 line:92%
Next up, Ted Cruz is thinking,

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This is the first picture
in my life

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I've had
the best-looking face."

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.547 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.315 line:92%
And finally, Obama is thinking,

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How did this dude get to be
40 years old

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.386
without learning the difference
between a cake and a cookie?"

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.088 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, you guys,
Christmas is just a week away,

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:20.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a lot of people are just
getting around

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
to doing
their Christmas shopping.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.595 line:92%
It can be a little stressful.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:25.365
So here to help with some
last-minute Christmas gift ideas

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
please welcome
our holiday correspondent,

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.835 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Julio Torres, everybody.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.670 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi. Hello.
-So great to see you.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
Julio Torres, everybody. Hey.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:39.145 line:92%
-Hello, Jimmy, and ho, ho, ho.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:39.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right, Julio,
last time you were here,

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had some
Halloween costume ideas

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were very conceptual
and almost impossible to get,

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I would say.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Yes, Jimmy.
I heard the feedback.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:50.390 line:92%
So none of that this time.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just very, very easy ideas
anyone can get.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.560 line:92%
-Okay. Okay, great. Go ahead.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.528 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Okay, first gift idea.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've heard of tree skirts,
right?

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Well, how about tree pants?

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:03.136
Because even though
all Christmas trees are ladies,

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.138 line:92%
some of them like to wear pants.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay. Here's another idea.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:12.345
A miniature bridge that connects
your ear with your lover's ear

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:15.882
so that your hopes and dreams
can enter his head at night.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.583 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:20.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Julio, these seem to be
kind of hard to find.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Well, how about
something easier,

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.326 size:88% position:44%
like chandelier earrings
with little open flames?

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because no one ever said
beauty was easy.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.029 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or how about a golden hand
mirror that shows you

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
the reflection of your rival
when you say,

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Show me the girl"?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.741
-Julio, how about something
that people can order online?

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:45.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, sure. Like a platypus
that's like, "Guess what.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bisexuality is real,
and so am I."

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.717 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:53.886
Or a locket with an old picture
of a soldier

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
who you've never met and yet
seems familiar but how?

00:05:58.191 --> 00:05:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What about, like, something
like socks or something?

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why would anyone need socks,
Jimmy? No, no, no.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
How about instead a music box
that can only be locked

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:12.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the inside
by the ballerina?

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:13.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:17.844
Or an autographed picture of me
in a little bullfighter outfit.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't pretend you're not dying
to see that.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know a few people who would
love that, yeah.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or a big, gorgeous hat
you can wear

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:28.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
and slowly tilt up
to reveal your face

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:33.726
like Kate Winslet in "Titanic."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or -- okay, how about a coffee
table book of your niece

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
posing for Christmas tree
pictures like this?

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:44.771
And of course -- okay, this one
might be a little obvious,

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:48.474
but a locked little door that
comes with a small mail slot

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:51.477
through which tiny letters
appear every now and then,

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:52.178 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but you can't open them

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:55.114
because they're addressed to
Umberto and that's not you.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:58.050 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
What about just, like,
a nice candle?

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:06.192
-Jimmy, no. People are going to
think you're weird.

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:09.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it up for "Tonight Show"
holiday correspondent

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:11.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
Julio Torres.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:12.965 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your hands --
They're a little wet.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A little clammy.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:17.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A little clammy,
not that clammy.

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Julio Torres right there.
Thank you, buddy.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:25.511 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:28.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally, you guys, I read that
marijuana-infused wines

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
are coming to states
with legal weed.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:33.519
Yep, something that makes you
drunk and high at the same time.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then Nyquil said, "Uh, hello!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:39.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots!

